# agentic-trader — droplet crontab template.
#
# ⚠️ FIRST INSTALL ONLY:  crontab deploy/crontab.template
# On the ALREADY-DEPLOYED box, do NOT run that — the live crontab carries box-only
# jobs this file does not (moomoo-vol-desk 9:30/9:35, moomoo-data-collector 16:30)
# and a wholesale install WIPES them. Arm a new job by APPENDING the single line,
# then `diff` the before/after. See docs/DEPLOY.md Phase 4.
#
# ⚠️ EDITING THIS FILE ARMS NOTHING. It documents intent; `crontab -l` is the
# source of truth. "Schedule X" is not done until the line shows in `crontab -l`.
# (Missed twice: 2026-07-20 universe refresh, 2026-07-24 signal panel.)
#
# Times are in the droplet's local TZ — set the box to US/Eastern or convert.
# ⚠️ Do NOT put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here or anywhere — it forces per-token billing.

# Cron runs with a bare PATH; give it node/npm (claude), python, git, coreutils.
# `which claude` on the box will confirm the right dir if claude isn't found.
#
# ⚠️ /root/.local/bin IS LOAD-BEARING — that is where `codex`, the independent
# reviewer, lives. It was missing here until 2026-08-13, so every INTERACTIVE
# test of the reviewer passed (a login shell has that dir) and the first and only
# CRON run failed with "ionice: failed to execute codex: No such file or
# directory". `claude` survived the same gap purely by accident of living in
# /usr/bin. Anything installed per-user (pipx/uv/npm --prefix ~/.local) needs
# this dir; verify a new dependency with `env -i PATH=<this> command -v <bin>`,
# NOT with `which` in your own shell — your shell is not what cron gets.
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin:/root/.local/bin
# Auth: Claude uses the interactive login stored in /root/.claude.json (from
# `claude` + `/mcp`). No CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN needed — do NOT set a bogus one.
HOME=/root

# --- SLOW LOOP (pure Python, no Claude) ---
# Weekly full rebalance: Sunday 20:00 — fetch fresh prices, re-rank, write the book.
0 20 * * 0   /opt/agentic-trader/deploy/run_slow_loop.sh >> /opt/agentic-trader/logs/slow.log 2>&1

# --- WEEKLY moomoo SIGNAL PANEL (system python3 — moomoo needs 3.10, not .venv) ---
# Sun 20:15, after the 20:00 rebalance writes the new book. Forward-logs a
# signal_panel journal event per held name for later meta-labeling. Non-fatal.
# `timeout 900` is the OUTER guard. The script bounds itself with SIGALRM
# (COLLECT_TIMEOUT), which is what produces the phone alert; this is the
# belt-and-braces for the case where a C-level call masks the signal. A healthy
# run takes ~2s, so neither bound is anywhere near the happy path.
15 20 * * 0  cd /opt/agentic-trader && timeout 900 /usr/bin/python3 scripts/collect_signals.py >> /opt/agentic-trader/logs/signals.log 2>&1

# Nightly risk-exit recompute: Mon–Fri 18:00 (after close).
0 18 * * 1-5 /opt/agentic-trader/deploy/run_slow_loop.sh >> /opt/agentic-trader/logs/slow.log 2>&1

# --- FAST LOOP --- MOVED TO A SYSTEMD TIMER 2026-08-14 ---
# Now deploy/agentic-fastloop.timer -> agentic-fastloop.service (Mon-Fri 10:00).
# ⛔ DO NOT RE-ADD A CRON LINE FOR IT. Both would fire and it PLACES ORDERS —
# the same plan executed twice. `systemctl list-timers` is the source of truth.

# --- DAILY EQUITY LOG (post-close, feeds mandate.drawdown()'s close-to-close series) ---
# Mon–Fri 16:15 ET — deliberately its OWN entry, not folded into the fast loop
# (10:00 ET, 32min after the open — the noisiest stretch of the session; the
# mandate promises close-to-close, never intraday) or the slow loop (would
# couple the equity track record to the book rebuild succeeding, and the
# Sunday 20:00 rebalance would write a spurious weekend point duplicating
# Friday's marks). 16:15 matches this codebase's settled-session boundary —
# see _drop_unsettled_session() in scripts/fetch_prices.py. See scripts/log_equity.py.
15 16 * * 1-5 cd /opt/agentic-trader && .venv/bin/python scripts/log_equity.py >> /opt/agentic-trader/logs/equity.log 2>&1

# --- INTRADAY RISK REVIEW — RETIRED 2026-08-13, folded into the sessions ------
# Was: 12:00 + 15:45 ET headless Claude de-risk overlay, armed 2026-07-15.
#
# ⛔ DO NOT RE-ADD without re-reading this. It was not removed for cost; it was
# SUPERSEDED, and the record is unambiguous:
#
#   37 runs BEFORE the session runner existed -> 3 orders intended
#    3 runs AFTER  the session runner went live -> 0 orders intended
#   40 runs total: 93 `watch` no-ops, 7 stop tightens, 3 trims.
#
# All three trims predate 2026-08-12. It has placed nothing since sessions
# began, because the sessions do the same work with judgment: the open/close
# sessions assess the book, re-anchor stops, and de-risk into events (measured
# 2026-08-13 — a session exited a name into an after-close print unprompted,
# and caught that the mechanical loop had re-bought it, which this overlay
# would not have noticed).
#
# Nothing else covered by it is now uncovered: market_monitor.py watches every
# stop and target CONTINUOUSLY through RTH, which strictly dominates a twice-
# daily snapshot; and there is no extended-hours trading, so the last decision
# that matters is the 15:15 close session, not a 15:45 pass 15 minutes before
# the bell.
#
# Removing it also DELETES A RACE: this overlay and the close session both
# read-modify-write monitor/overrides.json with no shared lock, and that
# interleaving was measured DROPPING a protective stop. One writer fewer.
#
# scripts/risk_review.py, prompts/risk_review.md and deploy/run_risk_review.sh
# were DELETED 2026-08-14 — they had sat unwired since the retirement and were
# the last thing describing a job that no longer runs.
# ⚠️ WHAT WENT WITH THEM: `risk_review.py --facts` was the only producer of the
# earnings_soon / near_stop / giveback / vol_expansion / ma_break flags in
# src/controls.py. Nothing consumed them (controls.py has never been wired to
# run live), which is why it was safe to delete — but if controls.py is ever
# wired, those five flags have NO producer and must be rebuilt, not re-enabled.

# --- AGENT SESSIONS (the inversion) - the agent decides, LIVE 2026-08-12 ---
# Supervision (lock, brief, process group, integrity tripwire, verdict) lives in
# scripts/session.py. Orders pass the PreToolUse gate declared in
# deploy/loop_settings.json: kill switch, order cap, universe whitelist,
# live_approved. Kill switch = touch research_store/HALT.
#
# deploy/run_session.sh MUST be executable (100755). A 100644 deploy makes cron
# fail at exit 126 BEFORE alert.sh installs the ERR trap - no phone push, no
# health check, the slot silently does nothing.
#
# Times are constrained by MEASUREMENT, not preference:
#  10:35 - originally because run_fast_loop.sh ran 10:00-~10:04 and two Claude
#          processes in research_store at once took the droplet down. That loop
#          was DELETED 2026-08-14, so the constraint is gone; the time is kept
#          only because it lets the open settle before the agent reads prices.
#  15:15 - the last decision point that matters: there is no extended-hours
#          trading, so whatever is held at 16:00 goes through the overnight gap.
#          (Until 2026-08-13 this also had to land before risk_review at 15:45,
#          because both read-modify-write monitor/overrides.json with no shared
#          lock and the interleaving was measured DROPPING a protective stop.
#          That overlay is retired, so the race is gone — but keep 15:15: it
#          leaves the session its full 1200s budget before the close.)
#          Do NOT "tidy" these onto the same minute.
#
# --- MOVED TO SYSTEMD TIMERS 2026-08-14 ---
# deploy/agentic-session@open.timer   -> agentic-session@open.service   10:35
# deploy/agentic-session@close.timer  -> agentic-session@close.service  15:15
# ⛔ DO NOT RE-ADD CRON LINES. Both would fire, and a session PLACES ORDERS.
#
# Why they moved: these jobs had NO resource limits and the fast loop had NO
# timeout at all — a wedged `claude -p` would sit indefinitely, and only the
# ASSUMPTION that a 10:00 job ends by 10:04 kept it clear of the 10:35 session.
# The units carry a real bound (TimeoutStartSec) and memory limits that throttle
# before they kill, and systemd refuses to start a unit already running, which
# replaces lock code we would otherwise maintain ourselves.


# --- WEEKLY INVESTOR LETTER (headless Claude narrative, then email) ---
# Sunday 21:00, after the slow loop writes the new book — the letter wraps the
# week and previews Monday's rotation. Emails only once NEWSLETTER_* creds
# exist in .env; until then it just writes research_store/newsletters/.
0 21 * * 0   /opt/agentic-trader/deploy/run_newsletter.sh >> /opt/agentic-trader/logs/newsletter.log 2>&1

# --- NIGHTLY LEDGER BACKUP (catch-all in case a run's inline backup missed) ---
30 22 * * *  cd /opt/agentic-trader && deploy/backup_ledger.sh >> logs/backup.log 2>&1

# --- DAILY UPKEEP CHECK (the reminder channel) ---
# 08:00 daily. Pure-Python, no Claude, places nothing. Checks that every scheduled
# job left a fresh artifact and that the Schwab token isn't about to expire, then
# pushes to the OPS ntfy topic (job names + ages only — never positions or P&L).
# Fire-once per condition; the dashboard carries standing status.
# REPLACED deploy/reauth_reminder.sh, which nagged every Monday whether or not you
# had already re-authed and never escalated if you missed it. This one reads the
# real token age, so it is silent when you're current and speaks up when you're not.
# --open-issue: also files/comments a deduped `bug`+`auto-fix` GitHub issue
# ("🔴 Scheduled job unhealthy") for the same fire-once conditions, feeding the
# claude.yml oversight loop. Never breaks the push if `gh` fails — see
# scripts/health_check.py.
0 8 * * *    cd /opt/agentic-trader && .venv/bin/python scripts/health_check.py --open-issue >> logs/health.log 2>&1

# --- WEEKLY UNIVERSE REFRESH (Piece 1) — every Friday 17:00 ET ---
# ⚠️ WAS QUARTERLY (`0 19 1-7 1,4,7,10 *` + a `date +%u`==7 guard in the wrapper,
# i.e. the first Sunday of Jan/Apr/Jul/Oct). Changed 2026-08-20: the candidate
# pool the agent selects from was being rescreened four times a year on paper
# and, in practice, NEVER — armed 2026-07-20, zero fires.
# 17:00: after the 16:00 close, before the 18:00 slow loop, so Friday's ranking
# already sees the fresh pool. The DAY is not enforced here — it lives in
# `[universe_maintenance] screen_day` and the script checks it itself.
0 17 * * 5   /opt/agentic-trader/deploy/run_universe_refresh.sh >> /opt/agentic-trader/logs/universe.log 2>&1
